DESCRIPTION:[Podcast: This Week in Virology]\n\nIn his weekly clinical upd
 ate\, Daniel Griffin and Vincent Racaniello continue their ongoing exasper
 ation over 5 deaths in Pennsylvania associated with measles infections\, t
 he absurdity of RFK Jr.’s statement that AI is better informed than phys
 icians\, the outbreak of cholera\, more deaths by raw milk products\, spre
 ad of dengue virus in Florida\, Ebola in DRC\, refusal to acknowledge the 
 benefits of the HBV vaccine birth dose\, how TORCH agent infections impact
  neurodevelopment and may lead to increase chances of autism diagnosis\, L
 egionnaires disease and screw worm cases\, before Dr. Griffin deep dives i
 nto recent statistics on RSV\, influenza\, SARS-CoV-2 infections\, the con
 tinued measles outbreak in Pennsylvania\, US\, and Canada\, modeling predi
 ctions of the outcome for repealing measles vaccination requirements to en
 ter school in Florida\, reactogenicity of different COVID vaccines and con
 tacting your federal government representative to stop the assault on scie
 nce and biomedical research. Click arrow to play Download TWiV 1362 (32 MB
  .mp3\, 53 min) Subscribe (free): Apple Podcasts \, RSS \, email Become a&
 nbsp\; patron &nbsp\;of&nbsp\;TWiV! Links for this episode A.I. Is ‘Bett
 er Informed’ Than Doctors\, Kennedy Tells Industry-Backed MAHA Summit (N
 Y Times) WHO reports latest global trends in cholera \, meningitis and pla
 gue (WHO) WHO: Global cholera deaths rose by 30% in2025 (CIDRAP) E. coli&n
 bsp\;Outbreak Linked to Raw Milk Cheese (CDC: E. coli infection) CDC confi
 rms multistate outbreak of\n\nEvent URL: https://www.microbe.tv/twiv/twiv-
 1362/\n\nSource: twiv_podcast
